1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,225
Click the pencil on B1, the sink base, to open the cabinet editor.

2
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:11,031
Settings on the left; a live 3D model and every part of the cabinet on the right.

3
00:00:11,031 --> 00:00:29,297
Rename it, then type the size. Inches can be typed as fractions.

4
00:00:29,297 --> 00:00:39,468
The 3D model updates right away. Drag in the 3D view to orbit around it.

5
00:00:39,468 --> 00:00:51,537
Explode pulls the parts apart so you can see how the box goes together.

6
00:00:51,537 --> 00:00:56,495
Fronts hides the doors, so you can look inside the cabinet.

7
00:00:56,495 --> 00:01:02,289
Materials: pick the board for the carcass, the back and the doors.

8
00:01:02,289 --> 00:01:16,566
Construction: toe kick height and setback, top rails, bottom joint, joinery.

9
00:01:16,566 --> 00:01:20,106
Back panel: grooved in, rabbeted, or applied to the back.

10
00:01:20,106 --> 00:01:25,662
The parts list: every panel with its cut size, material, edgebanding and machining.

11
00:01:25,662 --> 00:01:30,823
Click Done to go back to the job. The card shows the new size.
